@cc [owner:Nils-Fedrigo,label:security] client-transports-share-request-resolution
Every client-side transport helper in `client.ts` MUST obtain its target URL, headers and
credentials mode from `resolveRequest`, and MUST NOT call `getBaseUrl` or `getDefaultInit` itself
nor re-derive any part of that resolution. A transport that resolves its own URL or auth context
drifts from the others as soon as one of them changes, and silently loses the caller's credentials
(Bearer token in the browser extension, cookies in the SPA).
